{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00554",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 5.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Right shoulder's still playing up. Thought I'd better come back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.37,
      "end_seconds": 18.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "Right, let's see where we are with it. Is it the same pain as before, or has anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.03,
      "end_seconds": 26.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Same. The pain in my shoulder catches when I reach up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.24,
      "end_seconds": 34.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "And how long has it been going on this time round?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.48,
      "end_seconds": 39.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Three weeks. About that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.07,
      "end_seconds": 55.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "Oh, it's longer than that, love. You were rubbing it at the barbecue and that was ages ago. Six weeks, easily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.83,
      "end_seconds": 60.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Was it? Felt like three."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.72,
      "end_seconds": 70.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "All right, so somewhere between three and six weeks. What makes it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.73,
      "end_seconds": 74.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Lifting. Overhead stuff, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.44,
      "end_seconds": 80.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Anything that eases it? Heat, resting it, tablets?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.33,
      "end_seconds": 88.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Paracetamol takes the edge off. Nothing else."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.7,
      "end_seconds": 99.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Okay. Last time you also had that tingling in your fingers. Where's that got to?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.33,
      "end_seconds": 103.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Gone. Settled a while back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.58,
      "end_seconds": 110.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Do you remember when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.27,
      "end_seconds": 116.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "No idea, honestly. It was just there one day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 117.74,
      "end_seconds": 125.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Don't ask me. He never says a word until it's a problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.0,
      "end_seconds": 133.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Fair enough. Any fall or knock to the shoulder in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.92,
      "end_seconds": 136.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.55,
      "end_seconds": 143.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Any chest pain, or pain travelling up into the jaw?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.49,
      "end_seconds": 147.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Nope. Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.66,
      "end_seconds": 158.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Good. What are you taking at the moment? Include anything from the chemist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.39,
      "end_seconds": 168.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Ramipril, 5 milligrams once a day, for my high blood pressure. Paracetamol when it's bad. And the omeprazole."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.47,
      "end_seconds": 173.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "What strength is the omeprazole?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.05,
      "end_seconds": 176.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "20 milligrams. Every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.65,
      "end_seconds": 183.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Any allergies to medicines that I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.19,
      "end_seconds": 187.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 189.42,
      "end_seconds": 195.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "None that I know of, and I'd know by now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.96,
      "end_seconds": 200.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Have you had any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.67,
      "end_seconds": 206.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Appendix. About twenty years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.65,
      "end_seconds": 214.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "And does anything run in the family where shoulders are concerned?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.05,
      "end_seconds": 222.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "My dad had a frozen shoulder. Round about my age."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.35,
      "end_seconds": 232.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Right. Sit still for me and I'll do your blood pressure and pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.3,
      "end_seconds": 254.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "134 over 82, and your pulse is 72. Perfectly acceptable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.11,
      "end_seconds": 280.68,
      "duration_seconds": 15.57,
      "text": "Now lift that arm out to the side for me, nice and slow. Keep going up. There, you catch halfway. That's a painful arc as the arm comes out sideways."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.55,
      "end_seconds": 284.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Yeah. That's the spot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.29,
      "end_seconds": 301.03,
      "duration_seconds": 14.74,
      "text": "So, options. We can do an X-ray, we can do an ultrasound scan, or we can stick with exercises and wait. What would you rather?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.05,
      "end_seconds": 303.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Whichever's quickest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.06,
      "end_seconds": 316.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "Then let's get a shoulder X-ray booked for this week, and reception will ring you with the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.88,
      "end_seconds": 320.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.57,
      "end_seconds": 333.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "If it's still sore after the X-ray and a fortnight of exercises, we might do an ultrasound scan on top. Not before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.27,
      "end_seconds": 344.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "In the meantime, no heavy lifting above shoulder height, and go through the exercise sheet twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 346.98,
      "end_seconds": 350.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I'll make sure he does them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.19,
      "end_seconds": 354.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I'll manage, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.24,
      "end_seconds": 367.25,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "Good. Mind that shoulder on the way out, and don't let the door swing back on it."
    }
  ]
}
